UNANIMOUS WRITTEN CONSENT OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS

APOLLO DEFENSE TECHNOLOGIES CORP., - DELAWARE GENERAL CORPORATION LAW SECTION 141(f)

With unanimous consent, being all the members of the Board of Directors of APOLLO DEFENSE TECHNOLOGIES CORP., a Delaware corporation (the 'Corporation'), hereby unanimously consent in writing by the Board of Directors to the following payment to Section 141(f) of the DGCL:

SERIES B PREFERRED STOCK FINANCING RESOLUTIONS:

THEREAS, the Board deems it to be in the best financial interests of the Corporation and its stockholders to issue and sell up to 12,500,000 shares of Series B Preferred Stock at a purchase price of $ 4.80 per share, for an aggregate proceeds of $ 60,000,000.00, pursuant to the Series B Stock Purchase Agreement presented to the Board;

NOW THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, that the Certificate of Incorporation of the Corporation be amended and restated in its entirety (the 'Restated Certificate') to increase the authorized Common Stock to 120,000,000 shares into the authorized Preferred Stock to 35,000,000 shares, par value $0.0001 per share;

FURTHER RESOLVED, that the Chief Executive Officer, the Chief Financial Officer, and the Secretary are each authorized to execute and deliver the Series B Purchase Agreement, the Investors' Rights Agreement, the Right of First Resale and Co-Sale Agreement, and the Voting Agreement on behalf of the Corporation;

FURTHER RESOLVED, that an aggregate of 3,500,000 shares of Common Stock be newly reserved for issuance under the 2024 Equity Incentive Plan for key engineering personnel.
